        },
        {
            "summary": "Self-signed certificates for testing purposes",
            "explanation": "Self-signed certificates are digital certificates that are signed by an entity that is not recognized as a trusted certificate authority. They are commonly used for testing purposes, as they allow for the creation of a secure connection without the need for a trusted certificate authority. In this community, self-signed certificates are associated with HTTPS, suggesting that they can be used in conjunction with HTTPS for testing purposes. This relationship highlights the importance of self-signed certificates in the development and testing of secure communication systems. [Data: Entities (718), Relationships (612)]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "nginx as a backend service utilizing HTTPS",
