            "summary": "Cryptographic hash function usage",
            "explanation": "The SHA-256 cryptographic hash function is used to generate a unique hash for the merged text, as indicated by the relationship between SHA-256 and Merged Text. This ensures the integrity and uniqueness of the data stored in the knowledge graph. The use of cryptographic hash functions in the community demonstrates a focus on data security and reliability. [Data: Entities (489, 435), Relationships (436, +more)]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "Mission execution and environmental conditions",
