        },
        {
            "summary": "Hierarchy-aware merging as a key process",
            "explanation": "Hierarchy-aware merging is a specialized process within the merging community, designed to gather fine-grained clauses towards the ideal size without cross-topic pollution. This process highlights the focus on quality and precision in the merging process. The importance of Hierarchy-aware merging is further emphasized by its connections to Fine-grained Clauses, Target Ideal, and other related constraints [Data: Entities (1898), Relationships (1793, 1794, 1795, 1796, 1797, 1798, 1799)]."

        },
        {
            "summary": "Fine-grained clauses and constraints as essential components",
